---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { loadBoard } from "../lib/content";
import { formatDateTime } from "../lib/time";

const { settings, contactHref } = loadBoard();
---

<BaseLayout title="Methodology" description="How Libya Global Reports verifies, labels and limits its coverage.">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">Methodology</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This board is a human-edited briefing, not a live wire or a scoring engine. It answers four questions: what
      changed, where it matters, what the operational implications are, and what to watch next.
    </p>

    <h2>Verification</h2>
    <p>
      Collected RSS items and any future API excerpts enter a draft queue only. They are not published until an editor
      writes a structured article with sources, confidence and a verification status. Scraped or model-generated text
      never goes live on its own.
    </p>
    <p>
      Status labels: <strong>reported</strong> (single source or attributed claim), <strong>corroborated</strong> (independent
      confirmation), <strong>disputed</strong> (conflict recorded), <strong>corrected</strong>, or <strong>unverified</strong>.
      Missing data is shown as “No verified update” or “Not reported”. That is not a finding that conditions are normal.
    </p>

    <h2>Confidence</h2>
    <p>
      High, medium or low confidence is an editorial judgement with a short rationale on each article. It is not a
      probability, risk score or certainty claim.
    </p>

    <h2>Severity and direction</h2>
    <p>
      Severity and direction-of-change are qualitative labels for scanning. They are not gauges, indexes or forecasts.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a published fact is wrong, the article stays up with a correction history rather than disappearing. Substantial
      errors should be summarised in the correction line with a timestamp in Africa/Tripoli.
    </p>

    <h2>Currency comparisons</h2>
    <p>
      Official and parallel quotes are shown by location. A parallel-market premium is calculated only when the official
      and parallel observations share a currency pair and unit and their observation times fall within {settings.fxAlignmentHours} hours:
      ((parallel rate / official rate) − 1) × 100. This site does not invent a nationwide parallel rate. Observation time
      is kept separate from collection time. Stale rows are labelled.
    </p>

    <h2>Infrastructure and oil</h2>
    <p>
      Electricity, water and internet rows are incident notes, not comprehensive outage monitoring. Brent is labelled
      separately from Libyan crude grades. Commodity prices are omitted when no suitable feed exists.
    </p>

    <h2>Languages</h2>
    <p>
      The interface is English. Content records include a locale field so Arabic and RTL can be added later without
      rebuilding the data model. Logical CSS properties are used so direction can switch.
    </p>

    <h2>Coverage limits</h2>
    <p>
      Many official and operator sites have no verified public feed. Those sources stay in the register as disabled.
      The board will be thinner than a wire service and should be read that way. Last methodology review: {formatDateTime(settings.lastReviewedAt)}.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    {contactHref ? (
      <p><a href={contactHref}>Send feedback</a></p>
    ) : (
      <p>No contact address is configured yet. Set <code>LGR_CONTACT_HREF</code> or <code>contactHref</code> in settings. There is no unused form on this page.</p>
    )}

    <p><a href="/sources">Open the source register</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
